  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000102366,
      "SummaryText": "The Matt Brewing Company, its management and its employees are committed to operating in a manner that is safe for its employees and the community in compliance with Federal & State requirements.  As such, the Matt Brewing Company has established Risk Management & Process Safety Management Programs for  the Brewery.  This includes procedures for prevention of  accidental releases from the refrigeration system and the management of them should they occur.    \n\nThe Facility's operations are brewing and bottling/canning of malt beverages and sodas.  We refrigerate with closed loop Anhydrous Ammonia system to maintain appropriate temperatures for product brewing and storage. \n\nThe Brewery operates 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.  At all times a responsible Ammonia Refrigeration Engineer is on-site to respond to monitor system operation.  All employees that work with, or around the Anhydrous Ammonia refrigeration system have regularly scheduled training and additional training when appropriate or changes occur.\n\nThe Brewery's Ammonia Refrigeration system is fully diagramed on P&ID drawings.  Valves are also identified by tagging in conformance with the P&ID's .  Piping is identified by directional markings and information about contents and pressures. \n\nAn automatic system is used that detects and alarms.  A venting system automatically turns on in the event a leak of Anhydrous Ammonia is detected, and a notice is sent automatically to the Engineer's computer and Duty Engineers walk around phone.  The Ammonia refrigeration system can be shut down from the Engineer's computer in Boiler Room, control panel in Engine Room, or either of the two emergency stop buttons at the entrances to the engine room. \n\nEmergency planning & preparation for accidental release of Ammonia is carried out in coordination with our local emergency responders (LEPC)."
    }
  ]
